1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:03,002
THANK YOU FOR
THE DELICIOUS DINNER.

2
00:00:03,002 --> 00:00:04,880
YOU'RE WELCOME
FOR THE DELICIOUS DINNER.

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:07,048
HEY! WHAT ARE YOU GUYS
LOOKING AT?

4
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:09,760
Chandler:
ROSS AND THE MOST BEAUTIFUL
GIRL IN THE WORLD.

5
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,929
YEAH, COME TO PAPA!

6
00:00:17,518 --> 00:00:18,727
I KNOW!

7
00:00:20,813 --> 00:00:23,064
PROBABLY THE ONLY TIME
I'LL EVER SAY THIS

8
00:00:23,064 --> 00:00:25,693
BUT DID YOU SEE
THE ASS ON HER?

9
00:00:25,693 --> 00:00:28,111
WHERE DID YOU...?
WHEN DID YOU...?

10
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:29,321
HOW DID YOU...?

11
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:32,073
HOW DID YOU
GET A GIRL LIKE THAT?

12
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:33,659
YEAH, SO, WHAT IS SHE...

13
00:00:33,659 --> 00:00:35,118
LIKE, A SPOKESMODEL?

14
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:36,745
AEROBICS INSTRUCTOR? WHAT?

15
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:39,414
ACTUALLY, SHE'S A PALEONTOLOGY
DOCTORAL CANDIDATE

16
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:42,835
SPECIALIZING
IN THE CENOZOIC ERA.

17
00:00:42,835 --> 00:00:45,462
OKAY, BUT THAT'S, LIKE,
THE EASIEST ERA.

18
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:48,340
I'VE SEEN HER AT WORK

19
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:49,758
BUT I ALWAYS FIGURED...

20
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:50,801
( snorting )

21
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:54,763
BUT, UH, I MADE HER DINNER

22
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:56,264
WE HAD A GREAT TIME

23
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:58,350
AND WE'RE GOING OUT AGAIN
TOMORROW.

24
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:02,938
MAYBE SHE AND HER FRIENDS
ARE HAVING A CONTEST

25
00:01:02,938 --> 00:01:04,857
TO SEE WHO BRINGS HOME
THE BIGGEST GEEK.

26
00:01:04,857 --> 00:01:07,275
FINE BY ME.
HOPE SHE WINS.

27
00:01:13,991 --> 00:01:18,871
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

28
00:01:18,871 --> 00:01:21,373
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

29
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:23,709
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

30
00:01:23,709 --> 00:01:28,714
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

31
00:01:28,714 --> 00:01:30,340
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

32
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:33,928
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

33
00:01:33,928 --> 00:01:37,765
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

34
00:01:37,765 --> 00:01:40,059
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

35
00:01:40,059 --> 00:01:42,811
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

36
00:01:42,811 --> 00:01:44,688
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

37
00:01:44,688 --> 00:01:47,357
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

38
00:01:47,357 --> 00:01:51,152
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

39
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:59,160
HI. DO YOU GUYS HAVE
ANY WRAPPING PAPER?

40
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,997
OH! IS IT FOR
MY BIRTHDAY PRESENT?

41
00:02:01,997 --> 00:02:04,833
PHEEBS, IT WAS YOUR BIRTHDAY,
LIKE, MONTHS AGO.

42
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:07,168
YEAH, BUT REMEMBER YOU SAID
YOU ORDERED SOMETHING SPECIAL

43
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:09,421
AND IT JUST HADN'T COME YET?

44
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:13,884
WELL, I HAVE A CALL IN
ABOUT THAT.

45
00:02:13,884 --> 00:02:15,636
OH, OKAY.

46
00:02:15,636 --> 00:02:17,721
ACTUALLY, THIS IS FOR
KATHY'S BIRTHDAY.

47
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:19,556
IT'S AN EARLY EDITION
OF HER FAVORITE BOOK.

48
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:20,557
OH!

49
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:22,309
THE VELVETEEN RABBIT.

50
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:25,186
OH, MY GOD. WHEN THE BOY'S LOVE
MAKES THE RABBIT REAL...

51
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:26,688
OKAY, BUT DON'T TOUCH IT

52
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,983
BECAUSE YOUR FINGERS HAVE
DESTRUCTIVE OILS.

53
00:02:28,983 --> 00:02:32,152
OH. WELL, THEN YOU BETTER
KEEP IT AWAY FROM ROSS' HAIR.

54
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:37,491
THIS IS PRETTY RARE.
HOW DID YOU GET THAT?

55
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:39,701
IT WASN'T A BIG DEAL.
I JUST WENT
TO A COUPLE OF BOOKSTORES

56
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:41,703
TALKED TO A COUPLE OF DEALERS

57
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:44,915
CALLED A COUPLE
OF THE AUTHOR'S GRANDCHILDREN.

58
00:02:44,915 --> 00:02:47,126
OH... HONEY, THAT'S SO SWEET.

59
00:02:47,126 --> 00:02:50,420
YEAH, AND WHAT A GREAT WAY
TO SAY, "I SECRETLY LOVE YOU
ROOMMATE'S GIRLFRIEND."

60
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,341
IT DOESN'T SAY THAT.

61
00:02:54,341 --> 00:02:56,093
DOES IT?

62
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:58,553
HOW DO YOU THINK IT WILL
LOOK WHEN YOU GET HER

63
00:02:58,553 --> 00:03:01,222
SOMETHING INCREDIBLY
MEANINGFUL AND EXPENSIVE

64
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,892
AND HER BOYFRIEND JOEY
GIVES HER AN ORANGE?

65
00:03:05,393 --> 00:03:07,021
OKAY, I'LL JUST MAKE SURE

66
00:03:07,021 --> 00:03:09,106
JOEY GETS HER SOMETHING
REALLY GREAT.

67
00:03:09,106 --> 00:03:11,608
IT'S GOT TO BE BETTER
THAN THAT BOOK.

68
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:13,401
OOH! LIKE A CROSSBOW!

69
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:17,405
YEAH.
ONCE AGAIN, I AM SORRY.

70
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:20,199
THANK YOU. BYE.

71
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:22,201
I JUST HAD
TO TURN DOWN A JOB

72
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:24,454
CATERING A FUNERAL
FOR 60 PEOPLE.

73
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:26,373
( gasping ):
OH, MY GOD!

74
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:29,626
WHAT HAPPENED?
60 GUESTS.

75
00:03:33,463 --> 00:03:35,549
SO, UH, WHY'D YOU
HAVE TO TURN IT DOWN?

76
00:03:35,549 --> 00:03:37,676
BECAUSE I DON'T HAVE
THE MONEY OR EQUIPMENT

77
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:39,678
TO HANDLE SOMETHING THAT BIG
ON SUCH SHORT NOTICE.

78
00:03:39,678 --> 00:03:41,805
THERE'S NO WAY.

79
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:44,058
WHAT IS WITH
ALL THE NEGATIVITY?

80
00:03:44,058 --> 00:03:46,977
YOU SOUND LIKE "MONI CAN'T",
NOT "MONI CAN."

81
00:03:48,353 --> 00:03:51,606
"MONI CA."

82
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:55,610
YOU HAVE BEEN PLAYING AROUND
WITH CATERING
FOR OVER THREE YEARS.

83
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:56,987
DO YOU WANT TO BE
A CATERER OR NOT?

84
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:58,613
I DON'T KNOW.

85
00:03:58,613 --> 00:04:00,866
THERE YOU GO! THAT'S THE SPIRIT!

86
00:04:00,866 --> 00:04:04,536
NOW IF YOU NEED MONEY
I WILL LEND YOU MONEY.

87
00:04:04,536 --> 00:04:06,538
BUT JUST GET MOVING!

88
00:04:06,538 --> 00:04:10,125
REALLY? I NEED $500
FOR FOOD AND SUPPLIES AND STUFF.

89
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:13,587
IT'S WORTH IT
IF IT'LL GET YOU MOVING.

90
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:14,963
YOU HAVEN'T WORKED IN MONTHS.

91
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,215
YOU'RE NOT WORKING, EITHER.

92
00:04:16,215 --> 00:04:18,800
YES, BUT I'M DOING THIS.

93
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,511
THAT'D BE GREAT.
THANK YOU.

94
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:22,930
HEY.

95
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:25,390
HEY!
HEY.

96
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:28,227
CAN I BORROW THE KEYS
TO YOUR APARTMENT?

97
00:04:28,227 --> 00:04:31,230
WHY?
( chuckling )

98
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:34,024
YOU CAN PEE HERE!

99
00:04:35,192 --> 00:04:38,237
( chuckling nervously )

100
00:04:38,237 --> 00:04:40,239
YES, I CAN.
OF COURSE.

101
00:04:40,239 --> 00:04:41,907
IF YOU'LL EXCUSE ME.
IT'S OKAY.

102
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:43,867
THE DUCK'S USING
OUR BATHROOM ANYWAY.

103
00:04:47,412 --> 00:04:50,207
HEY, JOE WHAT ARE YOU GETTING
KATHY FOR HER BIRTHDAY?

104
00:04:50,207 --> 00:04:51,917
WE'VE ONLY GONE OUT
A COUPLE OF WEEKS.

105
00:04:51,917 --> 00:04:53,501
YOU THINK I'M
GETTING HER SOMETHING?

106
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:57,296
YES, YOU HAVE TO GET HER
SOMETHING REALLY NICE.

107
00:04:57,296 --> 00:04:58,924
OH! I KNOW.

108
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:00,884
AND NOT ONE OF YOUR COUPONS

109
00:05:00,884 --> 00:05:02,510
FOR AN HOUR OF "JOEY LOVE."

110
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:10,185
OOH! A CROSSWORD!
CAN I HELP?

111
00:05:10,185 --> 00:05:12,604
NO! I'M SORRY, HONEY.

112
00:05:12,604 --> 00:05:14,648
LAST WEEK, I GOT
ALL BUT THREE ANSWERS.

113
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,691
I WANT TO FINISH ONE
WITHOUT HELP.

114
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:18,359
FINE.

115
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:20,695
BUT YOU CAN'T HELP ME DEVELOP
MY NEW UNIVERSAL LANGUAGE.

116
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:25,533
HEY.
HOW'D IT GO?

117
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:28,287
OH, MY GOD!
IT WAS THE BEST FUNERAL EVER!

118
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,330
EVERYONE LOVED THE FOOD,
AND GUESS WHAT?

119
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:33,332
I GOT ANOTHER FUNERAL TOMORROW--

120
00:05:33,332 --> 00:05:36,335
THE DEAD GUY FROM TODAY'S
BEST FRIEND.

121
00:05:36,335 --> 00:05:39,006
IT IS LIKE
I AM THE OFFICIAL CATERER

122
00:05:39,006 --> 00:05:40,381
FOR THAT ACCIDENT.

123
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:42,341
GOD, I'M SO HAPPY FOR YOU!

124
00:05:42,341 --> 00:05:45,553
OH, THANKS.
CHECK OUT MY NEW
CATERING STUFF.

125
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:48,056
( gasping )
LOOK! I'M AN OMELET STATION!

126
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:50,309
"OMELET, MADE TO ORDER."

127
00:05:50,309 --> 00:05:52,351
( laughing ):
I'LL HAVE ONE, PLEASE.

128
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:53,728
PLUS MY MONEY.

129
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:56,273
OH.

130
00:05:56,273 --> 00:05:58,984
I DIDN'T REALIZE
YOU NEEDED IT BACK RIGHT AWAY.

131
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:00,652
YOU TOLD ME
TO GO BE A CATERER.

132
00:06:00,652 --> 00:06:03,947
SO I WENT, I BE'D.

133
00:06:03,947 --> 00:06:06,325
I USED IT TO BUY
ALL THIS STUFF.

134
00:06:06,325 --> 00:06:08,202
I GOT ANOTHER
JOB TOMORROW.

135
00:06:08,202 --> 00:06:09,870
I'LL PAY YOU BACK
WITH THE MONEY FROM THAT.

136
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,872
OH! OKAY.

137
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:13,332
OOH, SORRY I ACTED
LIKE A BANK.

138
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,467
HMM...
UM...

139
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:26,970
WOULD YOU LIKE TO COME IN?

140
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:31,432
DID HOMO ERECTUS HUNT
WITH WOODEN TOOLS?

141
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:34,853
ACCORDING TO RECENT FINDINGS.

142
00:06:34,853 --> 00:06:36,230
( both laughing )

143
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:37,689
( snorting )

144
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:48,658
HERE, MITZI!
HERE, MITZI.

145
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:50,160
UH...

146
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:51,953
MITZI IS...?

147
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:54,373
MY HAMSTER.

148
00:06:54,373 --> 00:06:57,084
I HOPE SHE'S OKAY.
I HAVEN'T SEEN HER IN A WHILE.

149
00:06:57,084 --> 00:06:59,211
HAVE A SEAT.

150
00:06:59,211 --> 00:07:01,713
( no audio )

151
00:07:01,713 --> 00:07:04,216
UH... OH, HEY!
DO YOU, UH...

152
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:06,467
( crunching )

153
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:11,472
DO YOU HAVE ANY, UM...
CINNAMON FRUIT TOASTIES?

154
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:15,476
WHAT?
WELL, I DO.

155
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:17,145
WHY DON'T WE GO BACK
TO MY PLACE

156
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:19,147
LIGHT A COUPLE OF CANDLES

157
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:22,650
BREAK OPEN A BOX OF
CINNAMON FRUIT TOASTIES.

158
00:07:24,194 --> 00:07:26,321
I'D RATHER NOT.
OH, YEAH?

159
00:07:26,321 --> 00:07:28,907
WHY NOT?
OKAY, UM...

160
00:07:28,907 --> 00:07:31,450
DON'T TAKE THIS THE WRONG WAY?

161
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:34,871
BUT YOUR PLACE KIND OF HAS
A WEIRD SMELL.

162
00:07:42,129 --> 00:07:43,755
IS EVERYTHING IN THE CAR?
YEP.

163
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:46,091
DID YOU SETTLE THE BILL?
NO.

164
00:07:46,091 --> 00:07:48,176
I HATE THIS PART.

165
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:51,305
( gasping ):
OH! LOOK WHAT WE ALMOST LEFT!

166
00:07:51,305 --> 00:07:53,472
THAT'S NOT MINE.
OH, ALL RIGHT.

167
00:07:53,472 --> 00:07:56,059
OOH! LOOK WHAT WE ALMOST TOOK!

168
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,484
EXCUSE ME, MISS BURKART.

169
00:08:05,484 --> 00:08:07,154
WELL, WE'RE ALL CLEANED UP
IN THE KITCHEN.

170
00:08:07,154 --> 00:08:09,823
OH, GOOD.

171
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:12,575
THANK YOU.

172
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:13,827
UM...
( clears throat )

173
00:08:13,827 --> 00:08:15,412
AND, WELL, THERE'S JUST...

174
00:08:15,412 --> 00:08:18,498
THE SMALL MATTER
OF THE, UM...

175
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:20,334
DEAR?

176
00:08:20,334 --> 00:08:22,919
JUST THE MATTER OF...
THE PAYMENT?

177
00:08:24,338 --> 00:08:28,467
JACK USED TO HANDLE
THE FINANCES.

178
00:08:28,467 --> 00:08:31,761
( sobbing )

179
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:37,267
( sighing )

180
00:08:40,228 --> 00:08:42,605
YOU KNOW WHAT WE SHOULD ALL DO?

181
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:44,774
GO SEE A MUSICAL.

182
00:08:47,361 --> 00:08:49,904
SURE.

183
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:52,657
AND YOU KNOW
WHICH ONE WE SHOULD SEE?

184
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:55,660
THE 1996 TONY AWARD WINNER.

185
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:59,622
DO YOU HAPPEN TO KNOW
THE NAME OF THAT ONE?

186
00:08:59,622 --> 00:09:01,166
I DON'T KNOW, UH...

187
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:03,084
GREASE?

188
00:09:03,084 --> 00:09:05,962
NO.

189
00:09:07,297 --> 00:09:09,007
RENT?

190
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:10,008
YES!

191
00:09:10,008 --> 00:09:11,718
RENT.

192
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:13,387
OKAY, SO WHEN DO YOU
WANT TO GO?

193
00:09:13,387 --> 00:09:15,972
WHAT? OH, I'M SORRY,
I CAN'T. I'M BUSY.

194
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:21,353
HEY.
HEY.

195
00:09:21,353 --> 00:09:24,605
MAN, IT IS SO HARD
TO SHOP FOR GIRLS.

196
00:09:24,605 --> 00:09:26,191
( groaning )

197
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:28,693
YES, IT IS--
AT "OFFICE MAX."

198
00:09:30,153 --> 00:09:32,155
WHAT DID YOU GET HER?

199
00:09:33,823 --> 00:09:36,576
A PEN.

200
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:41,248
IT'S TWO GIFTS IN ONE.
IT'S A PEN THAT'S
ALSO A CLOCK, HUH?

201
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:44,167
HA-HA!
YOU CAN'T GIVE HER THAT.

202
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:46,503
WHY NOT?
BECAUSE SHE'S NOT 11!

203
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:50,173
AND IT'S NOT THE SEVENTH
NIGHT OF CHANUKAH!

204
00:09:53,385 --> 00:09:57,680
HONEY, WHAT HE MEANS IS,
WHILE THIS IS A VERY NICE GIFT

205
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:00,308
MAYBE IT'S JUST NOT SOMETHING
A BOYFRIEND GIVES?

206
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:02,060
SURE, IT IS.

207
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:03,686
SHE NEEDS A PEN FOR WORK

208
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,313
SHE'S WRITING,
SHE TURNS IT OVER--

209
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:08,024
"WHOA! IT'S TIME FOR
MY DATE WITH JOEY!"

210
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:13,738
LOOK, WHAT DID YOU GET
FOR ANGELA DELVECCHIO

211
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:15,323
FOR HER BIRTHDAY?

212
00:10:15,323 --> 00:10:17,325
SHE DIDN'T HAVE A BIRTHDAY
WHILE WE WERE GOING OUT.

213
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:19,453
FOR THREE YEARS?

214
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:24,499
WELL, LOOK, IT'S TOO LATE,
AND I GOT AN AUDITION.

215
00:10:24,499 --> 00:10:27,461
( whining ):
I CAN'T SHOP ANYMORE!

216
00:10:27,461 --> 00:10:29,421
ALL RIGHT, I WILL GO OUT

217
00:10:29,421 --> 00:10:31,672
AND I WILL TRY TO FIND
SOMETHING FOR HER, OKAY?

218
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:33,674
THANKS, MAN.

219
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:36,219
OH, WHILE YOU'RE AT IT,
COULD YOU GET HER A CARD?

220
00:10:37,804 --> 00:10:40,723
WOULD YOU LIKE ME TO WRITE HER
A LITTLE POEM, AS WELL?

221
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:43,351
OR JUST GET A CARD
THAT HAS A POEM
ALREADY IN IT.

222
00:10:46,729 --> 00:10:48,523
YOU HAVE TO GET
OUR MONEY!

223
00:10:48,523 --> 00:10:50,525
PHEEBS, SHE COULDN'T
STOP CRYING.

224
00:10:50,525 --> 00:10:54,279
WITH THOSE THICK GLASSES,
HER TEARS LOOKED GIANT.

225
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:56,197
I KNOW IT'S TOUGH.

226
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:59,326
YOU KNOW THE FIRST THING I DID
AFTER MY MOTHER'S FUNERAL?

227
00:10:59,326 --> 00:11:01,328
WHAT?
PAY THE CATERER.

228
00:11:02,454 --> 00:11:04,581
LOOK, I'VE HAD
A LOT OF JOBS

229
00:11:04,581 --> 00:11:08,084
AND THERE ARE SOME PEOPLE
WHO JUST ALWAYS TRY
TO GET OUT OF PAYING.

230
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:10,711
IT'S EITHER, "THAT MASSAGE
WASN'T LONG ENOUGH"

231
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:12,713
OR, "I DON'T RECOGNIZE
ANY OF THOSE SONGS"

232
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,882
OR, "THESE SOMBREROS
AREN'T BIG ENOUGH.

233
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:17,511
BAD LITTLE WHITE GIRL."

234
00:11:18,595 --> 00:11:19,971
OKAY.

235
00:11:19,971 --> 00:11:21,973
SO YOU-YOU THINK SHE'S FAKING?

236
00:11:21,973 --> 00:11:25,768
IT SEEMS LIKE
THERE WEREN'T ANY TEARS
TILL YOU SHOWED HER THE BILL.

237
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:29,022
SHE SOUNDED PRETTY UPSET TO ME.

238
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:30,857
♪ YOU'RE A GRAND OLD FLAG ♪

239
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:32,400
♪ YOU'RE A HIGH-FLYIN' FLAG ♪

240
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:35,028
♪ AND FOREVER IN PEACE
MAY YOU WAVE... ♪

241
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:37,364
SHE SEEMS FINE NOW.

242
00:11:37,364 --> 00:11:38,823
♪ THE LAND I LOVE ♪

243
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:40,325
♪ THE HOME OF... ♪

244
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:45,955
SO YOU JUST LEFT?

245
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,624
HER PLACE WAS
REALLY THAT BAD?

246
00:11:47,624 --> 00:11:50,001
YOU KNOW HOW YOU THROW
YOUR JACKET ON A CHAIR

247
00:11:50,001 --> 00:11:51,710
AT THE END OF THE DAY?

248
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:53,880
LIKE THAT, ONLY
INSTEAD OF A CHAIR

249
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,549
IT'S A PILE OF GARBAGE.

250
00:11:57,467 --> 00:12:01,388
AND INSTEAD OF A JACKET,
IT'S A PILE OF GARBAGE.

251
00:12:01,388 --> 00:12:04,224
AND INSTEAD OF
THE END OF THE DAY
IT'S THE END OF TIME

252
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:07,435
AND GARBAGE IS ALL
THAT HAS SURVIVED.

253
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:10,397
HERE.

254
00:12:10,397 --> 00:12:12,357
WOW. THANKS.

255
00:12:12,357 --> 00:12:14,484
SO, UH, WHAT HAPPENED?

256
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:16,986
NOTHING HAPPENED.
I HAD TO GET OUT OF THERE.

257
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:19,614
ALL RIGHT. NEXT TIME,
YOU TAKE HER TO YOUR PLACE.

258
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:22,659
NO. I TRIED THAT.
SHE SAYS IT HAS A WEIRD SMELL.

259
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:24,411
WHAT KIND OF SMELL?

260
00:12:24,411 --> 00:12:27,038
I DON'T KNOW-- SOAP?!

261
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:30,041
ALL RIGHT. LISTEN, ROSS.
YOU LIKE THIS GIRL, RIGHT?

262
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:32,252
YOU WANT
TO SEE HER AGAIN?
YEAH.

263
00:12:32,252 --> 00:12:33,920
SO YOU'LL HAVE TO DO IT
IN THE MESS!

264
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:39,259
YEAH, OKAY.
YOU'RE RIGHT.
YEAH.

265
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:42,596
I MEAN, UH, WHO CARES
ABOUT A LITTLE SLOPPINESS?

266
00:12:42,596 --> 00:12:44,514
YEAH.
IT'S, UH...

267
00:12:44,514 --> 00:12:47,517
IT'S ENDEARING, REALLY.
ALL RIGHT.

268
00:12:47,517 --> 00:12:50,270
NOW, YOU GO GET
THAT BEAUTIFUL PIG.

269
00:12:51,688 --> 00:12:53,064
( snorts like pig )

270
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:01,698
OKAY, ALL RIGHT.

271
00:13:01,698 --> 00:13:03,157
I JUST SPENT
THE ENTIRE AFTERNOON

272
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,492
LOOKING FOR A PRESENT
FOR KATHY

273
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:06,785
THAT WOULD BE
BETTER THAN THE RABBIT.

274
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:09,205
ANY LUCK?
OH, YEAH.

275
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:12,791
I FOUND THIS GREAT PLACE CALLED
"INVISIBLE THINGS FOR KATHY."

276
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:14,961
CAN YOU GIVE ME A HAND
WITH ALL THIS STUFF?

277
00:13:14,961 --> 00:13:16,504
ALL RIGHT, LOOK.

278
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,673
WHY DON'T YOU JUST
RETURN THE BOOK

279
00:13:18,673 --> 00:13:20,841
LET JOEY GIVE HER THE CLOCK PEN
AND YOU GET HER SOMETHING

280
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:23,928
WORSE THAN THAT LIKE...
A REGULAR PEN.

281
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:28,600
SHE'S REALLY GOING
TO LOVE THIS, YOU KNOW?

282
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:31,394
THE BOTTOM LINE IS
I WANT HER TO HAVE IT

283
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:33,396
EVEN IF I DON'T
GET TO BE THE ONE

284
00:13:33,396 --> 00:13:34,855
WHO GIVES IT TO HER.

285
00:13:34,855 --> 00:13:37,024
OH, HONEY,
THAT'S SO SWEET.

286
00:13:37,024 --> 00:13:39,694
YEAH? YOU DON'T THINK
IT'S JUST PATHETIC?

287
00:13:40,737 --> 00:13:42,572
OOH! PATHETIC.

288
00:13:44,449 --> 00:13:47,494
HEY! I'M MEETING KATHY
IN TEN MINUTES.

289
00:13:47,494 --> 00:13:49,788
I BEEN LOOKING
ALL OVER FOR YOU.
WHERE?

290
00:13:49,788 --> 00:13:52,248
OUR PLACE, THE HALL! I...

291
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:58,338
I GOT SOMETHING FOR HER.

292
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:05,844
IT'S A BOOK.

293
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:08,348
A BOOK?

294
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:09,683
( gasps )

295
00:14:09,683 --> 00:14:11,976
IS IT, LIKE, A BOOK
THAT'S ALSO A SAFE?

296
00:14:14,312 --> 00:14:16,147
IT'S A BOOK;
JUST A BOOK.

297
00:14:16,147 --> 00:14:18,191
IT'S AN EARLY EDITION
OF THE VELVETEEN RABBIT.

298
00:14:18,191 --> 00:14:20,735
IT WAS HER FAVORITE
BOOK AS A KID.

299
00:14:20,735 --> 00:14:23,154
SO, UH, JUST LET ME KNOW
IF SHE LIKES IT, OKAY?

300
00:14:23,154 --> 00:14:24,614
OH, YOU GOT IT.
THANKS, MAN.

301
00:14:24,614 --> 00:14:26,825
THANKS FOR DOING THIS.
I OWE YOU ONE.

302
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:32,747
HEY! THERE WASN'T CHANGE
FROM THAT 20, WAS THERE?

303
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:37,210
NO. IT CAME OUT
TO AN EVEN 20.

304
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:42,006
WOW. THAT'S ALMOST AS MUCH
AS A NEW BOOK.

305
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:46,720
( brisk piano )

306
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:49,347
♪ JEEPERS, CREEPERS ♪

307
00:14:49,347 --> 00:14:51,516
♪ WHERE'D YOU GET
THOSE PEEPERS? ♪

308
00:14:51,516 --> 00:14:54,561
♪ JEEPERS, CREEPERS... ♪

309
00:14:54,561 --> 00:14:56,187
YOU DIDN'T GET
THE MONEY, DID YOU?

310
00:14:56,187 --> 00:14:59,482
MAYBE I CAN TRY AT INTERMISSION?

311
00:14:59,482 --> 00:15:01,818
OH, PHOEBE, COME ON.
LET'S JUST GO.

312
00:15:01,818 --> 00:15:05,029
NO! HEY, WE'RE NOT LEAVING
TILL WE GET PAID.

313
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:07,156
WHO DOES SHE THINK SHE IS?

314
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:08,949
ENOUGH IS ENOUGH.

315
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:11,745
HEY, WIDOW.

316
00:15:11,745 --> 00:15:13,496
♪ COME ON ALONG
AND LISTEN TO ♪
WIDOW?

317
00:15:13,496 --> 00:15:15,998
♪ THE LULLABY OF... ♪
EXCUSE ME. EXCUSE ME!

318
00:15:17,584 --> 00:15:19,043
THANKS.

319
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:22,547
UM, CLEARLY, THIS IS
A VERY, VERY HARD TIME FOR YOU

320
00:15:22,547 --> 00:15:26,801
UM, BUT WE PROVIDED A SERVICE
AND WE DESERVE TO BE PAID

321
00:15:26,801 --> 00:15:28,219
BECAUSE YOU ATE THAT SERVICE

322
00:15:28,219 --> 00:15:30,930
AND, UM, WE ARE NOT
LEAVING HERE

323
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,140
UNTIL WE ARE PAID EVERY PENNY,
'CAUSE YOU KNOW WHAT, LADY?

324
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:36,143
WE'RE PART-TIME CATERERS
AND WE HAVE NO PLACE ELSE TO GO.

325
00:15:38,229 --> 00:15:40,189
OH, ALL RIGHT.

326
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:42,525
I'LL GET MY BAG.
GOOD.

327
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:52,577
I'M GOING TO LEAVE
SOME CARDS HERE.

328
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:57,540
PLEASE THINK OF US
FOR YOUR NEXT EVENT.

329
00:16:04,088 --> 00:16:06,716
SO YOU WANT
TO COME INSIDE?

330
00:16:06,716 --> 00:16:08,301
( hesitantly ):
YES.

331
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,012
( firmly ):
YES, I DO.

332
00:16:21,606 --> 00:16:23,733
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE.

333
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:50,802
GUESS WHO?

334
00:16:50,802 --> 00:16:54,305
UH... DEPARTMENT
OF SANITATION?

335
00:16:55,765 --> 00:16:56,933
IT'S ME.

336
00:16:56,933 --> 00:16:59,519
OH. OH.

337
00:17:08,903 --> 00:17:11,322
OH!

338
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:12,490
WHAT?

339
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:14,241
OH, CHERYL!

340
00:17:14,241 --> 00:17:15,702
OH, ROSS!

341
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,454
OH! OH!

342
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:24,961
( wails )

343
00:17:24,961 --> 00:17:27,755
OH... GOD.

344
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:28,756
( rustling )

345
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:30,550
( yells )

346
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:36,263
OH, NO! NO!
NO, NO, NO!

347
00:17:36,263 --> 00:17:39,851
IT'S MY...
IT'S MY HAMSTER!
IT'S MITZI!

348
00:17:39,851 --> 00:17:43,604
OH, MY GOD. I'M SO SORRY.
I MUST HAVE FREAKED OUT.

349
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:45,398
OH, THANK GOD,
IT'S NOT MITZI.

350
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:47,984
( sighs )
IT'S JUST A RAT.

351
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:53,113
I DID IT.

352
00:17:53,113 --> 00:17:54,908
OH! I FINISHED IT!

353
00:17:54,908 --> 00:17:57,117
I DID IT ALL BY MYSELF!

354
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,119
AND THERE'S NOBODY TO HUG.

355
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:01,330
( clattering )
MOVE!

356
00:18:07,211 --> 00:18:09,463
HEY. HEY, YOU GUYS!

357
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:11,883
I FINISHED THE CROSSWORD
BY MYSELF. HUG ME.

358
00:18:11,883 --> 00:18:13,676
YAY! THAT'S SO GOOD.

359
00:18:13,676 --> 00:18:15,302
CONGRATULATIONS.

360
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:16,512
THANK YOU.

361
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,056
HOW'D THE CATERING GO?

362
00:18:18,056 --> 00:18:20,516
OH, IT WAS GREAT.
THE WIDOW WOULDN'T PAY

363
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:22,184
SO PHOEBE YELLED
AT HER TILL SHE DID.

364
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:25,145
YEAH. I'M A HARD-ASS.

365
00:18:25,145 --> 00:18:29,817
AND I'M A WUSS.
AND WE SHOULD BE PARTNERS.

366
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:32,737
YEAH-- HARDASS AND WUSS.
WE COULD FIGHT CRIME.

367
00:18:34,906 --> 00:18:36,741
WAIT A MINUTE, PHOEBE.

368
00:18:36,741 --> 00:18:38,158
WE SHOULD BE PARTNERS.

369
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:41,079
WE SHOULD BE CATERING PARTNERS.

370
00:18:41,079 --> 00:18:43,247
THINK ABOUT IT.
YOU'RE NOT WORKING
RIGHT NOW

371
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:45,249
AND WE HAVE SUCH
A GREAT TIME TOGETHER.

372
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,877
OKAY.
I COOK, YOU TAKE
CARE OF THE MONEY.

373
00:18:47,877 --> 00:18:50,254
OH! IT'LL BE LIKE
I HAVE A WIFE IN THE '50s.

374
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:52,381
( both screaming )

375
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:55,969
HEY.

376
00:18:55,969 --> 00:18:58,387
HEY. HOW'D IT GO?
HOW'D SHE LIKE THE GIFT?

377
00:18:58,387 --> 00:19:00,473
MAN, SHE LOVED IT.

378
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:02,140
SHE'S SHOWING MONICA
AND RACHEL NOW.

379
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:03,476
OH, YEAH? THAT'S GREAT.

380
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:05,061
LISTEN. I GOT
TO TELL YOU.

381
00:19:05,061 --> 00:19:07,354
I FEEL KIND OF BAD
TAKING CREDIT FOR THIS

382
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:09,148
BECAUSE, MAN,
AM I GOING TO GET

383
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,900
A LOT OF CREDIT FOR THIS.

384
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:12,485
( both chuckle )

385
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:16,196
HEY.

386
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:17,281
HEY.

387
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:19,408
HEY. HAPPY BIRTHDAY.

388
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:20,994
THANK YOU.

389
00:19:20,994 --> 00:19:23,496
YOU KNOW, UH, CHANDLER
GOT YOU A GIFT, TOO.

390
00:19:24,956 --> 00:19:26,624
NO, HE DIDN'T.

391
00:19:28,001 --> 00:19:29,418
YEAH, HE DID. LOOK.

392
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:31,587
IT'S RIGHT THERE ON THE COUNTER.
HO-HO-HO!

393
00:19:38,469 --> 00:19:40,680
HAPPY BIRTHDAY.

394
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,264
I'M SORRY.

395
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,853
YOU REALLY DIDN'T HAVE TO.

396
00:19:46,853 --> 00:19:48,270
WOW.

397
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,439
SEE, YOU THINK
IT'S JUST A PEN

398
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:54,152
BUT THEN YOU TURN IT OVER
AND IT'S ALSO A CLOCK.

399
00:19:54,152 --> 00:19:55,361
YEAH.

400
00:19:55,361 --> 00:19:57,071
NO. THIS IS GREAT.

401
00:19:57,071 --> 00:19:58,823
THANK YOU, CHANDLER.

402
00:19:58,823 --> 00:20:00,908
OH. Y-YEAH.

403
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:02,910
AH.

404
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,704
WANT TO GO TO BED?

405
00:20:04,704 --> 00:20:06,706
I'LL BE IN
IN A MINUTE.

406
00:20:06,706 --> 00:20:07,665
OKAY.

407
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:14,254
OH, UH, DON'T FORGET
YOUR COUPON.

408
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:22,388
GOOD NIGHT. 

409
00:20:22,388 --> 00:20:25,892
UM, THANK YOU FOR THE GIFT.

410
00:20:25,892 --> 00:20:27,476
OH, UH, YEAH.

411
00:20:27,476 --> 00:20:29,979
I JUST KNEW THAT SOMETIMES
WHEN YOU'RE WRITING

412
00:20:29,979 --> 00:20:33,941
YOU-YOU DON'T ALWAYS KNOW
THE EXACT TIME.

413
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:36,861
NO. I DIDN'T MEAN THE PEN.

414
00:20:36,861 --> 00:20:38,612
THANK YOU FOR THE BOOK.

415
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:41,240
UH, THE BOOK?

416
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,242
THE VELVETEEN RABBIT?

417
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:45,369
I HAVE THE FEELING YOU HAD
SOMETHING TO DO WITH IT.

418
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:47,245
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

419
00:20:47,245 --> 00:20:49,456
WELL, WHEN JOEY
GAVE IT TO ME

420
00:20:49,456 --> 00:20:51,625
HE SAID, "THIS IS 'CAUSE
I KNOW YOU LIKE RABBITS

421
00:20:51,625 --> 00:20:53,961
AND I KNOW
YOU LIKE CHEESE."
( sighs )

422
00:20:56,422 --> 00:20:59,258
THANKS. I LOVE IT.

423
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,260
AND I KNOW HOW HARD
IT MUST HAVE BEEN
FOR YOU TO FIND.

424
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,429
( mutters ):
OH, WELL.

425
00:21:03,429 --> 00:21:05,431
BY THE WAY, IN CASE YOU
MISSED THAT, THAT SOUND WAS:

426
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:07,975
( mutters ):
OH, WELL.

427
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:10,061
YOU MUST REALLY LIKE JOEY

428
00:21:10,061 --> 00:21:12,063
TO GO TO ALL THAT
TROUBLE FOR HIM.

429
00:21:12,063 --> 00:21:13,647
OH, YEAH! HE'S MY...

430
00:21:18,819 --> 00:21:21,447
HE'S MY BEST FRIEND.

431
00:21:21,447 --> 00:21:23,783
OH, WELL.

432
00:21:23,783 --> 00:21:25,952
GOOD NIGHT.

433
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:37,630
HEY, THAT COUPON EXPIRES,
YOU KNOW.

434
00:21:40,466 --> 00:21:41,926
( both giggle )

435
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:47,347
( knocking )

436
00:21:47,347 --> 00:21:49,850
HI. UH, YOU DON'T KNOW ME.

437
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,685
I'M MONICA GELLER,
ROSS'S SISTER.

438
00:21:51,685 --> 00:21:54,605
OH, YEAH. YOU KNOW,
IT'S TOO BAD
THAT DIDN'T WORK OUT.

439
00:21:54,605 --> 00:21:57,608
YEAH. ANYWAY, HE TOLD ME
ABOUT YOUR APARTMENT

440
00:21:57,608 --> 00:22:00,736
AND, UM, WELL...
I COULDN'T SLEEP
THINKING ABOUT IT.

441
00:22:02,655 --> 00:22:06,075
SO, UH, WOULD IT BE OKAY
IF I CLEANED IT?

442
00:22:08,202 --> 00:22:09,703
NO?

